Ambulance Route Optimization

A C++ project for optimizing ambulance routing using graph algorithms and optimization techniques.

Project Overview
This project implements efficient route optimization algorithms for ambulance dispatching and navigation. The goal is to minimize response times and improve emergency medical service delivery through intelligent path planning and resource allocation.

Features
Graph-based route representation
Shortest path algorithms (Dijkstra, A*, etc.)
Multi-stop route optimization
Real-time traffic consideration
Ambulance fleet management
Prerequisites
C++17 or higher
CMake 3.10+
GCC/Clang compiler
Standard C++ libraries

